    "result_text": "The full suite consists of just `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are support classes). All tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` rule following the project's existing conventions for derived owner fields.\n\n**Rule:** `membershipTier` = `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 **and** an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nTwo changes, mirroring how sibling derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`) are already done:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `membershipTier` property (read-only string enum `SILVER`/`BRONZE`) to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator produces the field and its `MembershipTierEnum` on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that returns `MembershipTierEnum.SILVER` when `namesakeCount != null && == 0` and email is non-blank, else `BRONZE`. The null-guard on `namesakeCount` avoids unboxing NPEs, and the enum type (rather than a raw `String`) satisfies the generated field's type.\n\nBoth endpoints (`POST /api/owners`, `GET /api/owners/{id}`) now return the field, and both acceptance tests \u2014 SILVER for a unique owner with email, BRONZE for an owner without email \u2014 pass.",
